ic and operational leadership for academic pathway in... View Details Bookmark Program Coordinator, Graduate Medical Education Founded in 1824, the GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences (SMHS) is the 11th oldest medical school in the country and the first in the nation’s capital. Since its establishment, the school has been at the forefront of medical education, and has grown to include highly-ranked programs in the health and biomedical sciences. With dozens of top-tier residency programs, SMHS is a competitive an... View Details Bookmark Senior Buyer The George Washington University’s Procure-to-Pay Department is responsible for the University’s procurement of goods and services, offering multiple purchasing methods via the iBuy+ system, electronic requisitions, and P-Cards. The department also manages supplier registration, travel, payables, and expense reimbursements through Concur. Our goal is to serve faculty and staff by facilitating t... View Details Bookmark Admissions Officer Founded in 1824, the GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences (SMHS) is the 11th oldest medical school in the country and the first in the nation’s capital. Since its establishment, the school has been at the forefront of medical education, and has grown to include highly-ranked programs in the health and biomedical sciences. With dozens of top-tier residency programs, SMHS is a competitive an... View Details Bookmark Senior Student Accounts Associate, Payments Functioning as one multidimensional team, the Controller’s Office is responsible for the overall integrity of the university’s fiscal activities. In that capacity, the Controller’s Office provides service excellence in all support and business operations to enhance the ability of the university to fulfill its vision of becoming one of the preeminent research universities in the nation and the w... View Details Bookmark Senior Administrative Assistant The Senior Administrative Assistant provides administrative support to the Office of Undergraduate Affairs and Special Programs and the Office of the Provost. The position reports directly to the Assistant Provost for Administration and Operations.This experienced administrative support position provides enhanced administrative support to one or more individuals. This position coordinates sched... View Details Bookmark Program Coordinator, Academic Operations To spark new thinking, just add friction. Your unique perspective and experiences can make you successful in your career.  About Us At the George Washington University’s College of Professional Studies, you’ll collaborate with a diverse group of experts from across disciplines and backgrounds, who will challenge you to rethink assumptions, test your ideas, and look at ways to make the greatest ... View Details Bookmark Zero Waste Specialist Position OverviewThe Zero Waste Specialist will lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of George Washington University’s zero waste and circular economy initiatives. This role is responsible for managing campus-wide waste diversion, reuse, composting, recycling, and materials management programs while supporting the university’s broader sustainability and operational g... View Details Bookmark Senior Office Assistant, Dean of Students Established in 1865, the George Washington University Law School is the oldest in the nation’s capital and one of the most prestigious law schools in the country. The Law School is accredited by the American Bar Association and is a charter member of the Association of American Law Schools. GW Law is situated in the tree-laden downtown Washington, DC, neighborhood familiarly known as Foggy Bott... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director, Career Counseling Established in 1865, The George Washington University Law School is the oldest in Washington, DC. The school is accredited by the American Bar Association and is a charter member of the Association of American Law Schools. The law school is located on the GW campus in the downtown neighborhood familiarly known as Foggy Bottom.The Career Center of The George Washington University Law School advi... View Details Bookmark UME Program Associate, Neurology Founded in 1824, the GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences (SMHS) is the 11th oldest medical school in the country and the first in the nation’s capital. Since its establishment, the school has been at the forefront of medical education, and has grown to include highly-ranked programs in the health and biomedical sciences. With dozens of top-tier residency programs, SMHS is a competitive an... View Details Bookmark Manager, Lerner Operations and Events The George Washington University and the Division for Student Affairs actively engages our students and our campus community through the spirit of healthy living and competition. Located in the heart of our nation’s capital, this world-class university aspires to have a world-class recreation program. We are committed to building and sustaining a program that mirrors the overall excellence of t... View Details Bookmark Senior Recruitment Partner Human Resource Management & Development (HRMD) is made up of several departments that serve as advocates for the GW community and consistently provide discreet, valuable and personalized service that is timely and responsive. HRMD helps GW to maintain a diverse workforce of the highest caliber and to support employees in their roles within the university.This senior position collaborates cl... View Details Bookmark Appliance Technician Facilities, Buildings & Grounds (FBG) is currently seeking an Appliance Technician to help support the Universities mission in education. FBG is a part of GW’s Facilities, Planning and Construction Management Division, which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses. Employees at GWU are offered a competitive salary, excellent benefits package, general retirement savings opt... View Details Bookmark Executive Director, Employee and Labor Relations The Executive Director, Employee and Labor Relations (ELR) provides leadership, strategy, direction and oversight for all labor (union) and employee relations (nonunion) functions across the university. In close collaboration with HR leadership and the Office of the Vice President and General Counsel (OGC) the Executive Director serves a key role in developing and advancing the university’s lab... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director, Admissions The Assistant Director, Admissions is responsible for coordinating and supporting recruitment, admissions, and enrollment activities for multiple undergraduate and graduate health sciences programs. This position serves as a primary point of contact for prospective students throughout the admissions process and works collaboratively with faculty, academic leadership, and university offices to e... View Details Bookmark Landscape Gardener, Equipment Operator Facilities, Construction, and Planning Management, under the Executive Vice President and Treasurer’s portfolio, manages and maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three of GW’s campuses. This includes housekeeping, routine and emergency maintenance, moving services, pest control, project management, life safety upkeep, HVAC repairs, grounds maintenance, and recycling/waste management.GW Fa... View Details Bookmark Fire Alarm Technician Facilities, Buildings & Grounds (FBG) is currently seeking a Fire Alarm Technician to help support the Universities mission in education. FBG is a part of GW’s Facilities, Planning and Construction Management Division (FCPM), which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses.Reporting to the Fire Alarm Shop Supervisor, the Fire Alarm Technician supports the Fire/Life Safety te... View Details Bookmark Associate Director, Employment Placement Established in 1865, The George Washington University Law School is the oldest law school in Washington, DC. The school is accredited by the American Bar Association and is a charter member of the Association of American Law Schools. The law school is located on the GW campus in the downtown neighborhood familiarly known as Foggy Bottom.The Career Development Office of The George Washington Uni... View Details Bookmark Police Sergeant The George Washington University Police Department is seeking highly motivated individuals for the position of Police Sergeant. Our goal is to be the premier university law enforcement agency in the region; best paid, best equipped and best trained. The GW Police Department is responsible for providing primary law enforcement and public safety service to a diverse university population of 25,00... View Details Bookmark Facilities Maintenance Technician Facilities, Buildings & Grounds (FBG) is currently seeking a Facilities Maintenance Technician (FMT) to help support the University’s mission in education. FBG is a part of GW’s Division of Safety and Operations, which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses. Employees at GWU are offered a competitive salary, excellent benefits package, general retirement savings options t... View Details Bookmark Associate Director, Employment Placement Established in 1865, The George Washington University Law School is the oldest law school in Washington, DC. The school is accredited by the American Bar Association and is a charter member of the Association of American Law Schools. The law school is located on the GW campus in the downtown neighborhood familiarly known as Foggy Bottom.The Career Development Office of The George Washington Uni... View Details Bookmark Employee & Labor Relations Manager We pride ourselves on being a champion to GW’s commitment to fair treatment of all members of its community and the main source of education to the university community on how to further our success and understanding of the value of a diverse workforce in our global environment.The Equal Employment Opportunity and Access office (EEOA) provides consultative services to assist staff with situatio... View Details Bookmark Electrician Facilities, Buildings & Grounds (FBG) is currently seeking an experienced, licensed Electrician to help support the university’s mission in education. FBG is a part of GWU’s Division of Safety and Operations, which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses.Reporting to the Facility Zone Manager, the Electrician typically maintains, repairs, and installs electrical systems an... View Details Bookmark Carpenter Facilities Buildings & Grounds (FBG) is currently seeking a Carpenter to help support the University’s mission and vision in Facilities Services. Facilities, Buildings and Grounds is a part of GWU’s Division of Safety and Operations, which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses. The work schedule for the Carpenter is 7:00 am to 4:00 pm, to include a Holiday and Weekend Ro... View Details Bookmark Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
